# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# TikuC: the same place to work, wearing its other name.  What differs
# is what it puts FORWARD -- no Run row, because nothing here runs a C
# program yet, and Build offered without being asked, because asking
# the compiler is what this program is for.  A project that names no
# target is asked about on this machine.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
expect-menu TikuC
menu-pick TikuC
wait 25
note it announces itself under its own name
expect-title TikuC
wait 200
expect-no-title TikuC
expect-title Project
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
expect-title Open
note the same scrollbar the folder windows wear, in the same place --
note and a press on its track PAGES the listing toward the hand
note the same scrollbar the folder windows wear, in the same gutter --
note and a press on its track PAGES the listing toward the hand
expect-pixel 722 230 d8d8d8
click 722 360
wait 8
expect-pixel 722 230 b1b1b1
click 722 215
wait 8
expect-pixel 722 230 d8d8d8
note the way UP heads the list itself: two clicks step into a folder,
note and the enclosing folder's row steps back out -- without it a
note panel that opened deep was a panel a person could not leave.  The
note machinery folders are not among the rows at all
click 400 200
wait 4
key Return
wait 20
click 300 165
wait 20
note back where it began, which the pick below can only make if so
click 400 240
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
note no Run row -- Add File… sits beside Build, and Build needs no
note target line to be offered.  And no About row here: that went
note where the system keeps its own, wearing this program's name
click-window Project
wait 8
note the system's menu wears the system's mark, right on the bar --
note one colour, the title's own ink, or at this size it is nothing
expect-pixel 13 5 000000
click 20 8
wait 8
expect-menu About TikuC
note and the desktop's own gestures are NOT on it -- Find, Preferences,
note Shut down are the desktop speaking, and the desktop is not who is
note in front.  Picking Preferences here reaches nothing, because the
note row is not there to pick
menu-pick Preferences…
wait 15
expect-no-title preferences
note a click on open ground puts the strip's menu away
click 500 600
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Open Project…||Build for host||Close Project
menu-pick Build for host
wait 200
expect-title Messages
key Down
wait 8
key Down
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Go to line 4
menu-pick Go to line 4
wait 120
expect-title bad.c
key x shift
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Save bad.c
wait 90
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/bad.c Xreturn nope
